<title>UK: Hard Rock in NBA talks for new chain--report.</title>
<headline>Hard Rock in NBA talks for new chain--report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hard Rock Cafe, part of Britain's Rank Group Plc, has held talks with the U.S. National Basketball Association (NBA) to create a global chain of cafes, the Sunday Times reported.</p>
<p>The newspaper said Hard Rock had been in talks with NBA commissioner David Stern for the past six months, with the rock-and-roll chain expected to provide business expertise in return for a basketball link.</p>
<p>However, a deal was some way off since Hard Rock was still talking to other potential partners, according to the paper.</p>
